  clock: 3  # 18b4
  nonce: 18b4  # 18b4
  message: "Fixed in PR (dev 592015ff19).\n\nBehavioral evidence, analyze_c on merged dev:\n- Fixture with tbl[] = { helper }, ops o = { .f = helper }, and (*cmds[])(int) = { helper }: `edge_source.unemitted_edge_sources` returns [].\n- dispatches_to edges are tbl -> helper, o -> helper, cmds -> helper, each src a kind=variable symbol.\n- user -> tbl and user -> cmds are dispatch_table references to those same symbols.\n\nCorpus, the item's own counter (dangling dispatches_to srcs):\n  crun  94 -> 0  (16 table variables emitted)\n  redis 505 -> 0 (85; dispatches_to 505 -> 509, dispatch_table refs 32 -> 51 from newly detected function-pointer arrays)\n  tmate 129 -> 0 (105)\nDownstream, run_behavior_map on crun: the edges were not merely masked as external_symbol but DROPPED. The map had 0 dispatches_to edges on dev and has 94 now, with 5 fewer external_symbol nodes.\n\nFix:\n- The table is emitted as a variable symbol, by the edges' own id and with a stable_id, once it holds a function. A data-only array is not emitted.\n- CAnalyzer collects the symbols per file in Pass 2.\n- An array of function pointers (static int (*cmds[])(int) = { f }), the item's \"seen on a fixture\" shape, is now detected through its function / parenthesized / pointer declarator wrappers.\n- test_c_call_anchor's pinned line now asserts no dangling src.\n\nNOT done: the cpp analyzer's own detector for the same function-pointer-array and designated-initializer shapes (the item's cpp note); cpp had 0 dangling srcs. Not filed separately yet: I have not checked whether cpp emits dispatches_to for those shapes on a fixture."  # 18b4
